course: dictionary
lesson: 14071
title: Wise sayings called maxims
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A maxim is a short, wise saying that gives a rule about how to behave or live. Most maxims are only one sentence long, so they are easy to remember. «Look before you leap» is a maxim: it reminds you to think before you act.
explain: Look for clues in the words around a maxim. Many maxims give advice and use words like "always", "never" or "best". «Honesty is the best policy» tells you that being honest is the right way to behave, even when a lie might seem easier.
explain: A character can live by a maxim. «Ruby's maxim was "Be kind, even when it is hard", so she always shared her lunch with the new girl.» Her actions show what the maxim means. When you meet a maxim, ask: what rule is it giving, and how does the character follow it?
explain: Maxim is close in meaning to proverb and motto. A proverb is an old, well-known saying, and a motto is a short saying a group or school lives by. Words with similar meanings can help you check your understanding, but they are not always exactly the same.
fact: A maxim is a short, wise saying about how to behave or live.
fact: «Honesty is the best policy» is a maxim about always telling the truth.
fact: «Look before you leap» is a maxim: think before you act.
fact: Maxims are close to proverbs and mottos, but each is a slightly different kind of saying.
fact: To check a maxim, ask yourself: what rule is this saying giving me?
exercise: «Look before you leap» is a maxim. What does it advise? | Jump as high as you can | *Think before you act | Always go first in a race
exercise: Mia's grandad says, «Honesty is the best policy.» What rule is he giving? | *Always tell the truth | Never eat sweets | Always win the game
exercise: Which of these is a maxim, a short wise saying about how to live? | The sun rises in the east each morning | My bike has two wheels | *Be kind, even when it is hard
test: «Her maxim was "Waste not, want not", so she never threw away good food.» What is a maxim? | A type of food | A long story about a king | *A short wise saying about how to behave
test: Which word is closest in meaning to maxim? | Riddle | Sunset | *Proverb | Paragraph
exam: «Ruby lives by the maxim "Be kind, even when it is hard."» What does a maxim give? | A list of ingredients for a cake | *A rule for how to behave | A map of a town | A type of weather
